# Purpose: the command palette's commands (Shortcut.PALETTE, Alt+P), as data with no UI code:
#          every action of the app you can run by name, as in VS Code's palette and Omarchy's
#          menu. Each has a group ("View: ..."), an icon, its shortcut when it has one, and
#          what running it does. A command with `slash` is also a slash command: typed as
#          "/<slash>" in the chat box, it runs exactly what its palette row runs (SLASH,
#          parse_slash; State.submit_chat). One with `takes` can be followed by text, eg "/vods
#          mkleo vs sparg0": its `slash_event` gets it.
# Usage: COMMANDS is drawn by ui.palette(); a new command is one row here. RUNNABLE is the
#        shortcuts Enter runs in the keybindings list (Alt+K, assets/keys.js).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
